    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d193">

                <pb facs="d192-02" n="2" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76ve06/d192-02"/>

                <head>193. Telegram 173878 From the Department of State
                    to the Embassy in Kenya<anchor n="1" xml:id="d193-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d193-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1976-07-14T01:05:00+00:00">July 14, 1976, 0105Z</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>From the Secretary for Ambassador Marshall</p>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>Subject:</label>
                    <item>Logistic flights and USS Ranger</item>
                </list>
                <list type="references">
                    <head>Reference:</head>
                    <item>Nairobi 7195</item>
                </list>
                <p>1. You may inform President Kenyatta on my
                    behalf that in light of the situation now existing in East Africa we have
                    stationed an aircraft carrier task force in the Indian Ocean. If Kenyatta is not immediately available to you,
                    you may pass this information to whomever you believe would be most appropriate
                    in terms of conveying it soonest to Kenyatta, but you should make sure it is understood as a message
                    from me to the President.</p>
                <p>2. You are authorized to make whatever arrangements are necessary for logistic
                    flights between Nairobi, Mombassa and the Ranger after you have passed the above
                    message.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        Kissinger
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d193-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d193-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, RG 59, Central Policy
                    Files, 1976. Secret; Niact Immediate; Nodis. Drafted by Blake, cleared by
                        Habib, approved by Eagleburger.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d193-f2" n="2" xml:id="d193-f2-content">
                <p>Secretary of State Kissinger instructed
                    Ambassador Marshall to inform President
                        Kenyatta that the United States had
                    stationed an aircraft carrier task force in the Indian Ocean.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
